## Context

A team project (No Country tech bootcamp) to build a platform where players find and reserve a football pitch in a few taps — and where pitch owners manage availability.

## Role

I led the UI design and front-end. I defined the interface in Figma and built it with the team in React + Tailwind, coordinating a cross-country group of developers and designers from idea to a working live product.

## Process

- Discovery — mapped the booking flow and the two sides of the marketplace: players reserving, owners listing.
- UI system — a clean, mobile-first design system in Figma: type scale, components, and the reservation flow.
- Build — translated the design into React + Tailwind components and wired the end-to-end reservation flow with the team.

## Outcome

Shipped a working, live product within the bootcamp timeline, coordinating a remote multidisciplinary team from first wireframe to a deployed booking flow players could actually use.
